   "text": "This structure is the decapeptide histrelin, pGlu\u2011His\u2011Trp\u2011Ser\u2011Tyr\u2011D\u2011His(Bn)\u2011Leu\u2011Arg\u2011Pro\u2011NHEt. I read it residue by residue from the left, and the first six assignments below come from the drawing:\n\n- **pGlu:** a 5\u2011oxopyrrolidine ring (lactam) whose carbonyl carbon is attached to the His residue.\n- **His:** an imidazole side chain with a free NH.\n- **Trp:** an indole side chain.\n- **Ser:** a CH2OH side chain.\n- **Tyr:** a 4\u2011hydroxyphenyl side chain.\n- **D\u2011His(Bn):** an imidazole side chain with a benzyl group on one ring nitrogen.\n- **Leu:** an isobutyl side chain.\n- **Arg:** a guanidine\u2011terminated propyl side chain.\n- **Pro:** a pyrrolidine ring, with the C\u2011terminus as an N\u2011ethyl amide (\u2011C(=O)NHCH2CH3).\n\nFor stereochemistry, I took every residue as L except the benzyl\u2011histidine, which I took as D. I assigned the @/@@ tags from the standard L\u2011amino\u2011acid pattern rather than re\u2011deriving each centre from the wedges and hashes. I adjusted the pGlu and Pro tags for their ring\u2011closure neighbour order.\n\nSMILES: O=C1CC[C@H](N1)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1c[nH]cn1)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1c[nH]c2ccccc12)C(=O)N[C@@H](CO)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1ccc(O)cc1)C(=O)N[C@H](Cc1cn(Cc2ccccc2)cn1)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCN=C(N)N)C(=O)N1CCC[C@H]1C(=O)NCC"
